WEBVTT

00:25.480 --> 00:27.400
'It's believed
that time stops for no one.'

00:28.920 --> 00:29.800
'That's right.'

00:30.520 --> 00:34.400
'Although time doesn't stop,
it can definitely change.'

00:36.040 --> 00:38.240
'And those who have
the skill to change it'

00:39.320 --> 00:40.840
'are visionaries.'

00:42.520 --> 00:45.240
'They're always
one step ahead of time.'

00:47.880 --> 00:50.120
'This is a story about people'

00:51.040 --> 00:54.280
'whose dreams and vision'

00:55.160 --> 00:58.800
'connected with countless wrists
across India.'

01:01.720 --> 01:04.760
Everyone warned me
about this decision,

01:07.880 --> 01:09.840
but I listened to no one.

01:14.200 --> 01:15.440
Now our company

01:17.320 --> 01:19.200
will be shut down.

01:20.880 --> 01:22.760
This happened because of me.

01:29.880 --> 01:30.680
I'm sorry.

01:34.320 --> 01:35.520
It's over.

01:48.120 --> 01:49.960
- An embodiment of hard work!
- Is the definition of a labourer!

01:50.000 --> 01:52.280
- If you want us to work...
- Take care of us!

01:52.400 --> 01:54.480
- An embodiment of hard work!
- Is the definition of a labourer!

01:54.560 --> 01:56.400
- If you want us to work...
- Take care of us!

01:56.440 --> 01:57.360
An embodiment of hard work!

01:57.400 --> 01:58.520
- Is the definition of a labourer!
- Is the definition of a labourer!

01:58.560 --> 02:00.800
- If you want us to work...
- Take care of us!

02:00.840 --> 02:02.800
- An embodiment of hard work!
- Is the definition of a labourer!

02:02.800 --> 02:03.840
If you want us to work...

02:04.720 --> 02:06.120
Where is Mr. Desai?

02:07.880 --> 02:09.360
If this continues, the Vashi Bridge

02:09.400 --> 02:10.760
won’t be completed
for a few more years.

02:10.840 --> 02:12.000
Why are you worrying?

02:12.440 --> 02:13.840
Let's find new workers.

02:14.200 --> 02:15.480
I'm sorry, sir,

02:15.600 --> 02:18.720
but changing the bottle
doesn't turn water into juice.

02:20.480 --> 02:22.160
What if the new workers
demand the same things?

02:22.200 --> 02:23.240
No! No! No!

02:23.520 --> 02:25.080
We cannot afford that.

02:25.400 --> 02:26.640
Exactly!

02:26.960 --> 02:28.960
Where the hell is Desai?

02:45.600 --> 02:46.680
If you want us to work...

02:46.720 --> 02:48.080
- Take care of us!
- Excuse me.

02:50.440 --> 02:53.160
They say, "An empty stomach
can't pray." Have you heard that?

02:53.920 --> 02:55.040
Likewise,

02:55.400 --> 02:57.920
you can't soften hard-hearted people
by getting wet.

02:58.080 --> 02:59.600
- What?
- Yes, it's true.

02:59.960 --> 03:01.800
The people sitting inside

03:02.120 --> 03:04.560
don't care about you
getting wet in the rain.

03:04.720 --> 03:07.840
However,
if these developers fall sick,

03:08.480 --> 03:09.960
who will protest tomorrow?

03:11.920 --> 03:14.640
Take an umbrella and then shout.

03:15.480 --> 03:21.080
Don't move
until your demands are fulfilled!

03:24.520 --> 03:26.520
- If you want us to work...
- Take care of us!

03:26.560 --> 03:28.040
Just a second. Sorry!

03:28.160 --> 03:29.760
Please change the slogan.

03:30.200 --> 03:33.440
- Excuse me! - This sounds
more like a Salim-Javed dialogue.

03:34.520 --> 03:35.440
Okay.

03:36.560 --> 03:39.040
- The embodiment of hard work...
- No! No! No!

03:39.440 --> 03:41.000
This... Uh...

03:41.920 --> 03:44.080
- Your slogan describes you.
- Yes.

03:44.280 --> 03:45.120
Not your demands.

03:45.760 --> 03:47.560
Speak about your demands.

03:48.760 --> 03:49.720
And...

03:51.160 --> 03:52.480
Please speak in English.

03:52.800 --> 03:56.000
They 'think' in Hindi,
but like to listen to English.

03:56.160 --> 03:58.520
But we can't speak English.

03:59.360 --> 04:00.200
Right?

04:00.680 --> 04:01.760
Right, my friends?

04:13.040 --> 04:15.360
- You discard!
- You discard!

04:15.880 --> 04:17.880
- We work hard!
- You discard!

04:18.160 --> 04:19.640
- Chin up!
- Pay up!

04:19.720 --> 04:20.960
- Chin up!
- Pay up!

04:21.040 --> 04:22.600
- Chin up!
- Pay up!

04:22.720 --> 04:23.760
Huh!

04:24.200 --> 04:25.520
Now they've started
protesting in English.

04:25.640 --> 04:27.680
Who taught them English?

04:27.800 --> 04:28.600
I did, sir.

04:28.720 --> 04:29.800
Mr. Desai?

04:29.960 --> 04:30.880
Present!

04:32.240 --> 04:33.560
I'm sorry. I'm late, sir.

04:34.520 --> 04:36.080
I was hunting for umbrellas.

04:36.440 --> 04:38.360
They had been getting drenched
in the rain for the past two days.

04:38.400 --> 04:39.240
Wow!

04:39.520 --> 04:41.000
We are praying

04:41.360 --> 04:43.880
that they stop protesting
because of the rain,

04:44.120 --> 04:45.480
and you're giving them umbrellas!

04:46.000 --> 04:50.320
My wife always says that,
between people and process,

04:50.520 --> 04:51.680
you should choose people,

04:51.760 --> 04:53.880
because they execute the process.

04:55.040 --> 04:56.600
Whose side are you on?

04:57.880 --> 04:59.000
I'm the project manager.

04:59.080 --> 05:00.760
I don't take sides.

05:01.320 --> 05:03.120
I see everyone as equal.

05:04.040 --> 05:05.040
"Saamaan?"

05:06.480 --> 05:07.560
'Saamaan'.

05:08.800 --> 05:09.680
No good?

05:11.160 --> 05:13.320
Sorry, I'm trying
to improve my Hindi.

05:15.560 --> 05:17.520
Equalise means 'saamaan'.

05:17.920 --> 05:19.240
- 'Samaan'!
- 'Samaan'!

05:20.000 --> 05:21.520
I treat them as equals.

05:22.640 --> 05:23.600
Huh? Good?

05:23.960 --> 05:25.440
Please tell me.

05:26.520 --> 05:28.160
What exactly is their problem?

05:28.240 --> 05:29.280
The problem is that

05:29.440 --> 05:31.640
the workers work for 12 hours,

05:31.680 --> 05:33.960
but want to be paid for 18.

05:34.000 --> 05:34.920
Not exactly.

05:35.440 --> 05:38.880
They work every day for 12 hours,

05:39.040 --> 05:40.680
and travel for 6 hours.

05:40.840 --> 05:43.160
It takes them 3 hours to get here
and 3 hours to return.

05:43.400 --> 05:45.000
That means they give us 18 hours

05:45.040 --> 05:47.320
out of the 24 in a day.

05:48.200 --> 05:51.920
And before they can
even rest after getting home,

05:52.000 --> 05:53.680
they start planning
for the next day.

05:53.800 --> 05:56.080
- So, try to put yourselves
in their shoes. - Look.

05:56.200 --> 05:59.360
These workers don't come here
on foot. They come by bus.

05:59.960 --> 06:03.040
They can sleep peacefully
while travelling.

06:04.080 --> 06:05.040
I have a solution.

06:05.760 --> 06:06.880
Please explain.

06:07.320 --> 06:08.440
Let's go for a walk.

06:08.800 --> 06:09.640
A walk?

06:10.400 --> 06:12.160
Yes. Certain things

06:12.600 --> 06:15.160
are understood through demonstration
rather than discussion.

06:15.600 --> 06:16.480
Come on, let's go.

06:18.920 --> 06:20.360
Okay! Let's go.

06:21.320 --> 06:22.600
You will need your umbrellas.

06:25.600 --> 06:27.800
- We work hard!
- You discard!

06:27.800 --> 06:30.200
- We work hard!
- You discard!

06:31.600 --> 06:33.400
Gosh! How much more?

06:36.760 --> 06:38.320
- Mr. Tiwari.
- Yes?

06:38.520 --> 06:39.920
This is your apartment, right?

06:40.760 --> 06:41.600
Right.

06:41.640 --> 06:43.360
Could you please open it?

06:52.240 --> 06:53.360
Nice!

06:54.560 --> 06:55.680
Very nice!

06:57.000 --> 06:57.880
It's spacious.

06:58.280 --> 07:00.080
Six people can easily fit in here.

07:00.440 --> 07:02.320
The next one is 102.

07:02.440 --> 07:03.400
That's mine, Desai.

07:03.480 --> 07:05.120
Right, and there are
six more over there.

07:05.160 --> 07:07.040
What is your point, Desai?

07:07.400 --> 07:09.600
We'll have to vacate this place.

07:09.680 --> 07:10.600
- What?
- What?

07:10.600 --> 07:13.200
- Do we have to vacate?
- What are you saying?

07:14.000 --> 07:16.200
If we want to stop this strike

07:16.280 --> 07:18.920
and complete
the Vashi Bridge on time,

07:19.160 --> 07:20.520
this is the only solution.

07:21.080 --> 07:23.360
We'll all leave, and our developers,

07:23.600 --> 07:25.240
whom you call workers,

07:26.320 --> 07:27.720
will move in here.

07:28.560 --> 07:29.400
Right?

07:40.240 --> 07:41.160
where will we go?

07:41.200 --> 07:42.520
- We'll move back into our houses.
- Huh!

07:43.000 --> 07:44.080
I will travel from Bombay,

07:44.160 --> 07:45.600
and you can travel from Pune.

07:46.200 --> 07:49.720
Desai, we live
four to five hours away from here.

07:49.920 --> 07:51.600
So how are we supposed to travel

07:51.680 --> 07:53.240
back and forth every day?

07:53.800 --> 07:54.920
Peacefully.

07:55.920 --> 07:57.400
I understand
what you're trying to say, Desai,

07:57.720 --> 07:59.000
but that is not possible.

07:59.120 --> 08:01.400
If you have another solution,
please tell me.

08:02.520 --> 08:03.640
Let's go for a walk.

08:05.280 --> 08:06.280
Again!

08:14.680 --> 08:17.640
If I had known,
I would have worn my sports shoes.

08:21.800 --> 08:23.760
Why have we come
to the Marketing Building?

08:28.960 --> 08:30.080
- Akash.
- Hmm?

08:30.400 --> 08:32.040
What is the area of this hall?

08:32.520 --> 08:35.920
Approximately 1,400 to 1,500 sq ft.

08:35.960 --> 08:37.280
"1,500 sq ft."

08:37.440 --> 08:39.920
If we build

08:40.280 --> 08:41.600
wooden partitions

08:41.680 --> 08:43.080
in these three places,

08:43.200 --> 08:45.800
we can have five rooms, right?

08:46.080 --> 08:48.120
- Hmm.
- How many such halls do we have?

08:48.160 --> 08:49.960
There are ten halls
and two vacant floors.

08:50.080 --> 08:52.600
So that's 20 halls,
with five rooms each.

08:52.720 --> 08:53.840
Which gives us...

08:53.960 --> 08:54.760
100 rooms.

08:54.920 --> 08:56.280
Nothing escapes you, sir.

08:59.080 --> 09:01.120
Our skilled developers
can stay here.

09:01.360 --> 09:03.480
We will need the Marketing Head's
permission for this.

09:03.960 --> 09:06.960
We will have to convince everyone
and obtain their signatures.

09:07.120 --> 09:09.000
It's a long and tricky process.

09:10.000 --> 09:11.200
It's not that tricky, sir.

09:12.080 --> 09:13.600
Everyone has already signed,

09:14.600 --> 09:16.480
and only yours is pending.

09:21.880 --> 09:24.320
I need to discuss this
with the board.

09:24.640 --> 09:25.680
Please, sir.

09:29.360 --> 09:30.160
Oi.

09:31.120 --> 09:33.360
If you already knew
about this place,

09:34.600 --> 09:35.960
why did you
take them to the quarters?

09:36.560 --> 09:38.920
I had to show them the bitter gourd

09:39.640 --> 09:42.080
to convince them to eat the okra.

09:44.960 --> 09:46.320
How could you?

09:46.720 --> 09:48.680
Anyway, I'm quite impressed.

09:48.720 --> 09:49.560
- Hmm?
- Hmm.

09:50.840 --> 09:52.720
But, Zee, they haven't agreed yet.

09:54.960 --> 09:58.320
Um, the workers...
I'm sorry, you're being too nice

09:59.040 --> 10:00.680
to the developers.

10:00.760 --> 10:01.600
Really.

10:02.280 --> 10:03.240
Uh, please.

10:11.040 --> 10:12.080
Please talk to them.

10:12.640 --> 10:15.480
I would love to,
but I don't belong to NBIDC.

10:15.520 --> 10:17.360
- It's fine. I'll take care of it.
- Okay.

10:17.880 --> 10:19.200
- Thank you, Akash.
- Good luck!

10:19.960 --> 10:20.760
Thank you, sir.

10:20.800 --> 10:21.680
- Desai.
- Yes.

10:24.120 --> 10:25.160
That was good.

10:25.600 --> 10:28.720
I'm thankful to have
borrowed you from Tata.

10:30.320 --> 10:31.480
Desai, I was thinking

10:32.560 --> 10:35.360
that every time we reached
a dead end in this project,

10:36.040 --> 10:38.480
you sought solutions for us.

10:38.920 --> 10:40.600
I think you deserve much more.

10:40.920 --> 10:44.040
More money, better policies,
and a secure future.

10:45.480 --> 10:48.640
One should at least have a
permanent job in this fleeting life.

10:50.800 --> 10:51.600
So,

10:52.600 --> 10:54.280
will you join NBIDC?

10:55.040 --> 10:56.040
Permanently?

10:57.840 --> 10:58.640
Come with me.

11:01.960 --> 11:03.800
Are you shocked or surprised?

11:05.960 --> 11:08.120
Sir, NBIDC is an incredible place,

11:08.880 --> 11:10.600
but the Tatas have sent me here

11:10.920 --> 11:12.640
on a five-year lease...

11:13.920 --> 11:15.360
I mean, I was lent to you.

11:16.240 --> 11:19.200
Today is the last day
of that contract.

11:19.440 --> 11:21.440
I know. That's why I'm asking you

11:22.120 --> 11:23.160
to join us.

11:23.280 --> 11:25.240
I'll get you promoted
in a few years.

11:28.720 --> 11:30.000
Desai.

11:30.480 --> 11:33.040
Thousands apply for this job

11:33.120 --> 11:34.840
and sit exams for years,

11:34.880 --> 11:36.600
yet they never make it here.

11:36.680 --> 11:40.080
I believe those people
deserve this job, sir.

11:42.560 --> 11:44.320
What does Tata offer you

11:44.680 --> 11:46.480
that NBIDC cannot?

11:47.080 --> 11:48.160
Peace.

11:49.400 --> 11:52.520
A person feels at peace
with their family.

11:53.320 --> 11:55.040
And Tata is family to me.

11:55.840 --> 11:59.240
A talented man like you
should work for the country.

11:59.280 --> 12:00.840
That's exactly what I
intend to do, sir.

12:02.680 --> 12:04.360
Thank you for your kind offer.

12:12.080 --> 12:13.080
Sir!

12:13.960 --> 12:15.040
The developers have agreed.

12:15.200 --> 12:17.360
Uh, they're bloody workers,
for God's sake.

12:21.160 --> 12:22.760
They agreed, but you didn't.

12:22.800 --> 12:24.000
Obviously!

12:24.840 --> 12:27.760
Please don't start your Hindi
classes in front of Rajini.

12:28.880 --> 12:30.760
She won't put up with you like I do.

12:30.960 --> 12:32.600
Are you jealous of Rajini?

12:32.960 --> 12:34.200
Do you want to marry me?

12:34.440 --> 12:35.720
You're not that lucky now.

12:36.560 --> 12:37.760
- I have my Kumud.
- Ooh!

12:38.240 --> 12:39.360
A heartbreak!

12:42.120 --> 12:43.600
But I'm so happy for you, Zee.

12:44.200 --> 12:45.960
Will you forget me?

12:47.440 --> 12:50.120
Akash, of course I will forget you.

12:50.720 --> 12:52.320
I'm not good
at long-distance relationships.

12:52.360 --> 12:54.320
Should I crash somewhere? Should I?

12:58.920 --> 13:00.400
Thank you!

13:01.400 --> 13:02.680
Argh!

13:05.800 --> 13:06.840
My pleasure!

13:09.280 --> 13:10.240
What happened?

13:13.840 --> 13:16.440
Someone once said

13:17.040 --> 13:18.480
we'd change the times together.

13:19.160 --> 13:20.400
Sounds familiar.

13:21.320 --> 13:23.000
But, sir, you're changing
the destination itself.

13:26.280 --> 13:28.880
"There's no destination in sight,
not even a trace of it."

13:29.680 --> 13:31.880
"Yet our journey continues."

13:33.480 --> 13:35.720
You said this quote without
referring to the Hindi dictionary!

13:39.040 --> 13:41.240
- Will you join Tata?
- Really?

13:42.160 --> 13:43.000
Are you serious?

13:43.320 --> 13:44.200
Zee!

13:44.360 --> 13:45.400
Answer me!

13:46.440 --> 13:47.640
Ta-ta!

14:10.320 --> 14:14.480
"My heart is restless."

14:14.760 --> 14:18.800
"I don't know who it will fall for."

14:19.120 --> 14:23.520
"My heart is restless."

14:23.560 --> 14:27.720
"I don't know who it will fall for."

14:37.600 --> 14:38.840
Did you leave the job?

14:39.040 --> 14:39.880
Yes, I did.

14:39.880 --> 14:40.720
Really?

14:42.440 --> 14:44.240
What should I call you now?

14:44.320 --> 14:47.040
Mr. Desai or Professor Desai?

14:54.680 --> 14:56.920
Are you joining the Tatas again?

15:00.200 --> 15:02.800
I thought you didn't want to work
in the corporate world anymore.

15:03.560 --> 15:06.440
I thought you wanted to fulfil your
dream of becoming a professor.

15:07.080 --> 15:08.600
Was that my dream?

15:08.640 --> 15:10.920
For that, you need
to understand yourself first.

15:11.560 --> 15:13.320
Only then can you
understand your dream.

15:13.400 --> 15:16.360
Ah, my guru!

15:17.480 --> 15:19.560
Here's your honorarium.

15:28.600 --> 15:29.720
How's the 'akuri'?

15:35.120 --> 15:36.840
"My heart is..."

15:36.880 --> 15:38.200
'- Mom!
- Mama!'

15:39.840 --> 15:40.920
Dad!

15:43.400 --> 15:44.800
My love!

15:46.520 --> 15:48.800
- Uh... Here you are!
- Ah!

15:50.400 --> 15:52.960
Wow, Mom! We have a guest today.

15:55.600 --> 15:58.360
Does a guest come
to your house and cook? Huh?

15:58.920 --> 15:59.920
A paying guest.

16:00.560 --> 16:02.120
"A paying guest?"

16:02.480 --> 16:03.440
Very smart.

16:04.240 --> 16:05.640
- Come here.
- No! No! No!

16:05.680 --> 16:07.120
Come here!

16:08.960 --> 16:11.440
Now, you won't have to travel
four hours to see me.

16:12.400 --> 16:14.320
So, you're finally becoming
a professor?

16:14.600 --> 16:15.440
Um...

16:20.400 --> 16:21.960
Tomorrow, I will take
a day off from school.

16:22.280 --> 16:23.720
- We'll go out to play.
- That's a good idea.

16:23.800 --> 16:24.880
- Yes.
- Listen up, hero!

16:25.200 --> 16:27.240
You go to school, not an office,
where you can take a day off.

16:27.640 --> 16:29.480
Your dad will be busy from tomorrow.

16:29.560 --> 16:30.840
Why? Where are you going?

16:32.000 --> 16:33.240
To meet his second family.

17:09.760 --> 17:12.560
Bye! Bye! Bye! Mwah! Bye!

17:12.960 --> 17:15.520
- Dad, your lunchbox!
- "Lunchbox!" Yes.

17:15.560 --> 17:18.080
- Dad, your lunchbox!
- Oh! "Lunchbox!"

17:19.800 --> 17:21.360
My lunchbox. Thank you!

17:22.760 --> 17:24.040
Good morning! Good morning!

18:00.840 --> 18:01.640
Where to?

18:01.840 --> 18:02.760
Office!

18:03.080 --> 18:05.920
- I know that, but who are you?
- Xerxes.

18:06.560 --> 18:07.480
What does that mean?

18:09.320 --> 18:11.360
It's a name. That's my name.

18:12.560 --> 18:14.000
It seems really old.

18:14.720 --> 18:15.840
Were you on holiday?

18:16.320 --> 18:18.000
Yes, a five-year-long holiday.

19:00.360 --> 19:01.080
Come in.

19:04.800 --> 19:05.680
Pinks!

19:06.200 --> 19:07.320
Desai!

19:07.680 --> 19:08.840
I've been expecting you.

19:08.920 --> 19:11.320
Ah! The burden of expectations.

19:13.520 --> 19:14.600
- Pinks.
- Hmm?

19:14.840 --> 19:16.080
Who has occupied my office?

19:16.400 --> 19:18.360
Ask Jeh about it.

19:18.560 --> 19:19.680
Only he can tell you that.

19:20.200 --> 19:21.160
Come with me.

19:25.040 --> 19:25.680
But, Pinks...

19:26.120 --> 19:27.320
Don't call me that.

19:27.520 --> 19:28.960
Only Mr. Tata can call me that.

19:29.040 --> 19:30.080
Okay, but where is he?

19:30.680 --> 19:32.360
- On a business trip.
- Oh.

19:32.880 --> 19:34.440
- He will be back today.
- Oh!

19:36.560 --> 19:38.960
This is your 'destination'.

19:40.080 --> 19:40.880
Oh!

19:41.360 --> 19:43.040
Do you need anything? Tea or coffee?

19:44.480 --> 19:46.040
I want my cabin back.

19:46.480 --> 19:47.560
You can't have it.

19:49.000 --> 19:50.680
At least give me some work.

19:54.680 --> 19:56.480
Please...

19:57.800 --> 20:00.640
Will you give me a chance

20:01.160 --> 20:02.480
- to help you?
- No.

20:03.120 --> 20:04.000
Thank you.

20:07.840 --> 20:08.640
Um...

20:09.040 --> 20:09.840
Hello!

20:09.880 --> 20:11.240
Sir, I have the sheets with me.

20:11.280 --> 20:12.200
Yes, sir. I have the numbers.

20:12.240 --> 20:13.800
We can start tallying them
right away, sir.

20:14.720 --> 20:16.280
Yes, sir. Yes, absolutely.

20:21.200 --> 20:22.520
Correspondence.

20:22.720 --> 20:24.640
It's not 'correspondance'. Right?

20:25.520 --> 20:28.760
Please mop at the corners. Okay?

20:29.920 --> 20:30.800
Do it properly.

20:32.640 --> 20:34.560
'Avsar' means opportunity.

20:37.720 --> 20:39.480
Sir, over here. Mr. Khanna.

20:39.560 --> 20:40.680
Over there as well.

20:41.960 --> 20:43.640
Yes, sir!
I wanted to discuss with you...

20:43.680 --> 20:44.880
There are plenty
of grammatical errors.

20:44.920 --> 20:45.760
Shall I retype it?

20:45.840 --> 20:46.800
No, thank you.

20:52.160 --> 20:53.920
- Sir.
- Yes?

20:54.320 --> 20:55.840
Where is Pinks?

20:56.080 --> 20:58.040
I think she went to meet Mr. Tata.

20:58.280 --> 20:59.120
Where?

21:08.360 --> 21:10.440
There he is, 001.

21:11.680 --> 21:12.920
I have heard of 007,

21:13.680 --> 21:15.000
but what's 001?

21:15.120 --> 21:16.440
It's Jeh's licence number.

21:16.600 --> 21:19.080
He is the first Indian
to get a pilot's licence.

21:19.480 --> 21:21.080
And he still flies himself.

21:22.440 --> 21:23.440
Incredible!

21:35.160 --> 21:38.280
Oh! My entire staff is here
as a welcome committee.

21:38.960 --> 21:40.280
- Ahuja Sahib.
- Welcome, sir.

21:40.320 --> 21:41.200
How are you?

21:42.480 --> 21:43.880
- Hello, Mr. Singh.
- Welcome, sir.

21:44.880 --> 21:46.520
- [in Gujarati] Zee, how are you?
- I'm great.

21:46.640 --> 21:49.040
This is Mr. Jim Edgar.

21:49.040 --> 21:49.960
Greetings!

21:50.560 --> 21:53.440
He works with the great
Martin Cooper.

21:54.680 --> 21:57.920
He had to come to India
for work, so I gave him a lift.

21:58.520 --> 22:01.960
In return, he gave me the chance

22:02.600 --> 22:06.400
to show you this prototype.

22:10.440 --> 22:14.480
This is the genius of Martin Cooper.

22:15.920 --> 22:18.160
A totally wireless cellphone.

22:19.520 --> 22:20.600
Have a look.

22:24.160 --> 22:26.720
Mr. Tata, I know

22:27.240 --> 22:29.160
this is a dream come true, but...

22:30.400 --> 22:32.360
Who will buy a cellphone?

22:32.440 --> 22:34.000
Only the wealthy.

22:34.080 --> 22:35.120
No, sir.

22:35.520 --> 22:36.400
No.

22:36.800 --> 22:38.880
Innovation is always expensive,

22:38.960 --> 22:41.440
but by the time it reaches
the distribution stage,

22:41.520 --> 22:43.360
it becomes affordable.

22:43.480 --> 22:44.400
- Right.
- Yes.

22:44.520 --> 22:47.920
For example, the car, the radio,

22:48.080 --> 22:50.280
the gramophone, or the telephone.

22:51.040 --> 22:54.960
In the beginning, all of these
were extremely expensive.

22:55.280 --> 22:56.440
But look now.

22:57.200 --> 23:01.240
Oi, Pinks,
'vishishtata' is expensive,

23:01.400 --> 23:03.640
but 'samaveshta' is affordable.

23:03.800 --> 23:04.640
What does that mean?

23:05.560 --> 23:08.080
What he means is that

23:08.400 --> 23:12.680
exclusivity is expensive,
and inclusivity is affordable!

23:12.760 --> 23:13.640
Yes!

23:16.240 --> 23:17.240
Thank you!

23:19.560 --> 23:21.000
Here you are. Thank you, Jim.

23:21.400 --> 23:22.440
Thank you, sir.

23:22.720 --> 23:23.880
There's a car waiting for you.

23:23.960 --> 23:25.440
- Thank you.
- I'll see you later.

23:25.680 --> 23:26.840
- Thank you, sir!
- Bye.

23:27.480 --> 23:28.360
Sir.

23:31.360 --> 23:33.760
We already have
a telephone in the market,

23:34.320 --> 23:37.880
so what's the need
for a wireless phone?

23:39.160 --> 23:40.280
Ahuja Sahib.

23:40.760 --> 23:41.640
Yes, sir.

23:42.000 --> 23:44.560
Do you remember when, last year,

23:44.840 --> 23:49.880
you had a multi-million dollar deal
to negotiate?

23:50.000 --> 23:51.960
- Of course, sir.
- And you

23:52.280 --> 23:54.680
needed my permission for that.

23:54.720 --> 23:55.840
An urgent permission.

23:55.920 --> 23:57.440
Of course, sir. Of course.

23:57.720 --> 23:59.000
It was a deal worth millions.

23:59.240 --> 24:00.720
- How could I forget that?
- Right.

24:01.400 --> 24:04.040
I was on a one-week tour back then,

24:04.680 --> 24:07.320
and since my schedule was
confidential, you couldn't reach me.

24:07.560 --> 24:09.000
Right! That's right.

24:09.240 --> 24:11.360
Now suppose I were

24:11.680 --> 24:14.080
carrying a telephone with me,

24:14.720 --> 24:16.920
neither of us would be
constrained by wires.

24:18.000 --> 24:20.080
No deal would have slipped
through your fingers.

24:20.840 --> 24:21.960
Mr. Tata,

24:22.640 --> 24:26.000
do you think we should enter
the cellphone business?

24:26.680 --> 24:30.160
Investing in any new innovation
is risky,

24:30.240 --> 24:34.320
but we can certainly
draw inspiration from it.

24:36.000 --> 24:37.600
But remember,

24:39.200 --> 24:42.000
having passion isn't enough.

24:43.400 --> 24:46.400
You must have an idea
that is feasible.

24:48.560 --> 24:49.760
That's all.

24:52.280 --> 24:53.320
Thanks.

24:53.640 --> 24:56.680
Sir...
Sir, I want to speak with you.

24:56.840 --> 24:57.920
- Get in!
- Okay.

25:02.280 --> 25:05.600
What have they done
to you at NBIDC, Zee?

25:05.680 --> 25:07.800
I'm not pathetic
because of NBIDC, sir,

25:07.880 --> 25:09.080
but because of you.

25:09.160 --> 25:10.320
Why? What did I do?

25:10.360 --> 25:11.920
You know how much I love my job.

25:12.160 --> 25:13.440
Yet you sent me there

25:13.520 --> 25:15.240
and found my replacement here.

25:15.560 --> 25:17.760
Only because of your experience.

25:17.840 --> 25:20.440
It was time for you
to get a promotion.

25:20.520 --> 25:22.880
"Promotion?" I sit around
doing nothing all day.

25:23.440 --> 25:25.600
Who works
on the very first day of a job?

25:25.840 --> 25:27.400
Please rest for a while.

25:28.760 --> 25:31.720
I need something exciting.

25:31.840 --> 25:32.920
I want a challenge.

25:33.480 --> 25:34.680
- Really?
- Hmm.

25:35.560 --> 25:36.800
Well, you're in luck.

25:37.240 --> 25:42.360
Because a challenge has been
waiting for you for a long time.

25:42.760 --> 25:43.600
Okay.

25:44.560 --> 25:45.680
The Tata Press.

25:47.080 --> 25:48.440
"The Tata Press?"

25:50.120 --> 25:52.000
It has been making a loss
for seven years.

25:52.080 --> 25:53.800
You said you wanted a challenge.

25:54.080 --> 25:56.280
This is not a challenge.
This is a death sentence.

25:57.560 --> 25:59.200
Zee, this is

26:00.600 --> 26:02.480
the most precious watch
in the world.

26:02.560 --> 26:04.160
It's a rare edition.

26:04.600 --> 26:07.600
Henry Andre,
the owner of Andre Jeuba,

26:08.000 --> 26:09.520
presented me with this watch.

26:09.600 --> 26:10.880
It's very dear to me.

26:11.320 --> 26:14.240
If you find a way
to recover Tata Press's losses,

26:15.120 --> 26:16.160
it'll be yours.

26:18.960 --> 26:20.160
Do you accept the challenge?

26:34.960 --> 26:37.160
- Good morning, my darlings.
- Good morning!

26:37.520 --> 26:38.600
It's for you!

26:38.920 --> 26:39.760
Thank you.

26:39.800 --> 26:41.200
Shall I drop you two off at school?

26:41.240 --> 26:42.840
- Yes, Dad.
- Come on, let's go.

26:42.920 --> 26:44.640
- Keep your plates in the sink.
- Yes.

26:44.760 --> 26:46.560
Wait... Hang on!

26:48.000 --> 26:49.920
Hmm! Where is...

26:52.600 --> 26:54.080
- Somebody is excited.
- Let's go, Dad.

26:54.160 --> 26:55.800
Somebody has a new challenge.

26:57.120 --> 26:58.040
Come on, let's go.

27:00.520 --> 27:02.240
Oh, my!

27:35.800 --> 27:37.000
Do you think
you'll be able to defeat me?

27:38.920 --> 27:39.760
Let's see.

27:40.960 --> 27:42.600
- Excuse me!
- Yes?

27:43.000 --> 27:44.160
Who's in charge here?

27:55.280 --> 27:56.680
Mr. Mody?

27:58.480 --> 27:59.880
You must be Mr. Desai.

28:00.120 --> 28:01.000
Yes.

28:01.800 --> 28:03.280
- Welcome!
- Thank you.

28:03.600 --> 28:04.600
Just a minute.

28:06.920 --> 28:09.680
Varun, please bring me
two cups of Rajwadi tea. Yes.

28:10.360 --> 28:12.800
Come with me, Mr. Desai.
Let me give you a tour of the press.

28:12.920 --> 28:15.480
No. I need all the press files.

28:19.920 --> 28:21.040
All the files?

28:21.200 --> 28:22.600
All the files.

28:24.200 --> 28:25.080
Oops.

28:25.320 --> 28:26.720
May I sit here?

28:26.880 --> 28:27.960
Uh, yes.

28:44.600 --> 28:45.520
Zee.

28:46.280 --> 28:48.320
It's 1 a.m. Come and sleep inside.

28:48.480 --> 28:49.920
Just two minutes.

28:50.480 --> 28:51.800
Wrap it up quickly.

28:57.520 --> 28:58.320
Thank you!

28:58.960 --> 29:01.400
I need the sales report
for the last five years.

29:03.600 --> 29:06.080
This is for the financial year
1978-79.

29:06.400 --> 29:09.160
'Tata Press gave Xerxes
sleepless nights,'

29:09.800 --> 29:11.400
'but he didn't know'

29:12.440 --> 29:14.600
'that in resurrecting it,'

29:14.920 --> 29:17.960
'he would discover a dream'

29:18.320 --> 29:20.240
'that would
keep him awake day and night.'

29:20.320 --> 29:21.840
Varun, please bring us Rajwadi Tea!

29:24.440 --> 29:25.920
- Morning... Morning! Good morning!
- Good morning.

29:26.000 --> 29:27.480
It might be a good morning for you.

29:28.040 --> 29:30.080
What is this Indus Script project?

29:30.800 --> 29:33.240
The most money was spent
on this project last year.

29:33.280 --> 29:35.640
The officials
from the Archaeological Department

29:36.200 --> 29:37.880
found some old scripts.

29:38.640 --> 29:41.000
They wanted
to preserve those scripts,

29:41.240 --> 29:43.240
and we wanted to save
the press's reputation.

29:43.400 --> 29:44.360
So, we took on the project.

29:44.480 --> 29:46.440
But why did we incur so much loss?

29:46.560 --> 29:49.080
Actually, what happened
was that, to print those scripts,

29:49.080 --> 29:51.240
we needed
new machines and new fonts.

29:51.640 --> 29:55.520
I thought Mr. Manoharan
would keep bringing in new projects,

29:55.720 --> 29:57.320
and our press's profits
would increase.

29:57.520 --> 29:59.560
Is he Shankar Manoharan?

29:59.680 --> 30:02.520
Yes! But unfortunately,
it was his last project.

30:02.880 --> 30:04.760
After that, we never saw him again.

30:12.000 --> 30:12.840
Hello, Operator.

30:12.880 --> 30:15.160
Please connect me to the Delhi
Archaeological Department.

30:18.280 --> 30:20.440
Hello! Is it the Delhi
Archaeological Department?

30:21.000 --> 30:23.760
Could I speak
to Mr. Shankar Manoharan?

30:25.240 --> 30:26.160
Transferred?

30:27.040 --> 30:28.560
Hello, Operator.
Could you please connect me

30:28.600 --> 30:31.040
to the Delhi Traffic Department?
Thank you.

30:32.240 --> 30:36.240
Hello! Yes. Could I speak
to Mr. Shankar Manoharan, please?

30:37.200 --> 30:38.080
Transferred!

30:40.400 --> 30:43.680
Operator, could you please
connect me to TIDCO in Madras?

30:46.000 --> 30:48.160
Hello, TIDCO? Yes.

30:48.200 --> 30:49.880
[in Hindi] Yes! May I speak...

30:49.920 --> 30:52.080
Could I please speak
to Mr. Shankar Manoharan?

30:54.920 --> 30:56.040
"Bombay?"

30:57.600 --> 30:58.440
Thank you.

31:04.840 --> 31:06.840
Do you realise how much...

31:06.880 --> 31:08.480
Where are my noodles?

31:09.680 --> 31:10.480
"Noodles?"

31:10.520 --> 31:12.040
Yes, I ordered it.

31:13.680 --> 31:15.040
You're the manager, right?

31:15.480 --> 31:17.160
Yes, I'm the manager.

31:17.240 --> 31:18.440
So where are my noodles?

31:19.240 --> 31:21.200
I ordered it an hour ago.

31:21.320 --> 31:23.520
We took the order a year ago.

31:24.400 --> 31:27.040
Yet we haven't received
a single order since.

31:27.800 --> 31:28.600
Sorry?

31:28.640 --> 31:31.720
I'm Tata Press's general manager,
not the hotel's.

31:32.800 --> 31:33.880
Oh!

31:34.480 --> 31:35.680
Oh my God!

31:37.800 --> 31:38.720
Nice to meet you.

31:38.880 --> 31:40.720
Nice to meet you. I'm Xerxes.

31:41.160 --> 31:42.240
- Shankar.
- Oh.

31:42.920 --> 31:44.480
Do you realise
how much money you've cost us?

31:44.760 --> 31:47.520
May I wear my clothes first?

31:47.880 --> 31:49.000
Actually,

31:49.080 --> 31:51.760
I don't hold meetings in a bathrobe.

31:54.560 --> 31:57.480
This is archaeological work, Xerxes.

31:59.000 --> 32:00.800
We don't necessarily

32:01.080 --> 32:02.200
find something every month.

32:02.280 --> 32:05.440
I agree, but what about
our business relations?

32:05.640 --> 32:07.840
You...
You were the last hope of the press.

32:07.960 --> 32:09.360
You don't know how much money...

32:12.400 --> 32:14.400
Why are you taking out
your frustration on me?

32:14.560 --> 32:15.520
Do you think

32:15.760 --> 32:19.800
I enjoyed searching
for ancient stones

32:19.840 --> 32:21.600
for the Archaeological Department?

32:22.400 --> 32:24.000
I thought

32:24.560 --> 32:25.960
history was your passion.

32:28.320 --> 32:31.600
I like working
for our country's progress,

32:31.840 --> 32:32.880
not for history.

32:33.480 --> 32:34.280
Ditto.

32:35.040 --> 32:38.000
Getting transferred
to the Archaeology Department

32:38.600 --> 32:40.880
was not my wish.
It was a punishment.

32:41.320 --> 32:42.880
- "Punishment?"
- Yes.

32:43.240 --> 32:44.080
But why?

32:44.120 --> 32:47.160
In my previous posting,
I used to deal with smugglers.

32:48.720 --> 32:51.400
Why are you staring at me?
It's true.

32:52.120 --> 32:53.440
- "Smugglers?"
- Hmm.

32:53.600 --> 32:55.200
However, I made a mistake.

32:55.800 --> 32:58.760
I confiscated the goods
of some shady people,

32:59.360 --> 33:02.120
and pressure from my superiors
led to my demotion.

33:04.040 --> 33:05.240
What did you confiscate?

33:05.440 --> 33:06.880
You cannot even imagine.

33:09.080 --> 33:09.880
Booze?

33:09.960 --> 33:11.920
Your imagination is far too limited.

33:12.280 --> 33:13.480
Diamonds?

33:13.960 --> 33:15.360
Gold? Drugs?

33:16.200 --> 33:17.560
- You can't guess.
- Wood?

33:18.240 --> 33:19.440
Animal skins?

33:19.720 --> 33:22.240
- Toothbrushes? - You'll be
saying "gallstones" next.

33:23.080 --> 33:25.800
- Human organs.
- Please stop it.

33:28.520 --> 33:29.680
Watches.

33:35.160 --> 33:36.120
"Watches?"

33:37.200 --> 33:39.400
Imported foreign watches.

33:41.240 --> 33:45.040
Everyone wants to wear them,
but not everyone can afford them.

33:47.720 --> 33:51.560
Because these watches
don't just show the time,

33:52.400 --> 33:55.000
they display the status
of the person wearing them.

33:56.440 --> 34:02.080
That's why watches are the most
smuggled item in our country.

34:03.440 --> 34:05.120
Its demand

34:05.680 --> 34:07.960
will never decrease. Mind it.

34:09.000 --> 34:09.960
Never.

35:08.040 --> 35:09.160
Ashok!

35:10.480 --> 35:11.320
Ashok!

35:12.160 --> 35:13.480
Sharma!

35:14.960 --> 35:16.760
- Varun!
- Yes, sir!

35:17.240 --> 35:18.720
Has everyone gone deaf?

35:19.840 --> 35:21.240
Why can't I see anyone?
Where's everyone?

35:21.360 --> 35:22.760
Sir, everyone has gone out!

35:30.840 --> 35:32.720
'Attention! Attention! Attention!'

35:32.840 --> 35:34.960
'Ladies and gentlemen,'

35:35.080 --> 35:38.160
'five sarees for just 50 rupees!'

35:38.680 --> 35:41.200
'Sale! Sale! Sale!'

35:41.280 --> 35:43.080
The rates will increase
during the festive season.

35:43.120 --> 35:43.920
That is for 300.

35:44.000 --> 35:46.680
This one is for 400,
but it's the latest design.

35:46.760 --> 35:48.560
- It'll look really good on
your wrist. - Mister, show me this.

35:48.680 --> 35:50.960
- Yes, sir. Let me show you the
latest design. - I'll give Rs. 300.

35:51.040 --> 35:51.960
- Mister.
- Yes.

35:52.040 --> 35:53.000
How much for this?

35:53.120 --> 35:54.120
This is for 800.

35:54.200 --> 35:56.680
Please wait, ma'am.
I'll give your watch. Here it is.

35:56.840 --> 35:57.920
It's too expensive.

35:58.520 --> 36:01.560
It's a watch, not soap.
There is a fixed rate.

36:01.640 --> 36:03.800
We don't bargain. The rates
will rise during the festival.

36:03.920 --> 36:04.760
So, buy now.

36:04.840 --> 36:05.920
The watches are really nice.

36:06.000 --> 36:07.120
Where do you get them from?

36:07.200 --> 36:08.560
Why are you wasting
my time, my friend?

36:08.600 --> 36:10.240
If you want it, buy it.
If not, just leave.

36:10.560 --> 36:12.880
Mister, what kind
of watches do you have?

36:13.000 --> 36:15.400
Sir, just tell me
which watch you want.

36:15.480 --> 36:18.720
We have all the watches.
Citizen, Seiko, Roamer, and Sandoz.

36:18.800 --> 36:20.240
Is this watch in demand?

36:21.520 --> 36:23.280
- Riyaz, please deal with him.
- Okay.

36:23.320 --> 36:25.240
- Please leave. Come on, leave.
- This one...

36:26.440 --> 36:28.640
What's your turnover?

36:28.800 --> 36:30.280
"Turn?" What do you mean?

36:30.440 --> 36:32.960
I mean, how much
do you earn in a day?

36:34.320 --> 36:36.520
Sonu, please deal with him.

36:40.400 --> 36:41.680
They threw me out, sir.

36:49.280 --> 36:50.560
Hello, Operator.

36:50.760 --> 36:53.960
Could you please connect me
to the New Bombay NBIDC office?

37:05.840 --> 37:06.880
'Done?'

37:07.200 --> 37:08.240
'It's the best.'

37:24.800 --> 37:25.920
Mister, I need a watch.

37:26.400 --> 37:27.720
- Which company?
- Swiss.

37:28.240 --> 37:29.200
You'll get it here.

37:29.920 --> 37:32.160
I need forty thousand watches.

37:34.960 --> 37:36.040
Forty thousand?

37:36.440 --> 37:38.040
I want to give those
as Diwali gifts to my employees.

37:38.720 --> 37:41.520
Listen,
I can only give you 40 watches.

37:42.240 --> 37:44.200
No problem. Thank you.

37:46.920 --> 37:47.760
Psst!

37:49.480 --> 37:50.800
I can get you the watches.

37:52.280 --> 37:53.080
You?

37:55.080 --> 37:56.560
Why are you joking? Let it be.

37:57.520 --> 37:58.560
I'm not joking.

37:59.880 --> 38:01.400
I have some good connections.

38:15.080 --> 38:17.240
Do you run a company?

38:17.680 --> 38:19.800
I have an arrangement
with the supplier.

38:21.920 --> 38:24.280
Please come
to this address at 9 p.m.

38:25.800 --> 38:27.200
Don't bring the police with you.

38:27.720 --> 38:29.520
Otherwise, it will backfire.

38:31.560 --> 38:32.640
Be there on time.

38:52.600 --> 38:53.840
Is this the right place?

38:54.560 --> 38:57.520
Yes, I think so.

39:02.240 --> 39:04.240
- Your name, please?
- Akash Dixit.

39:06.520 --> 39:08.720
- Do you both have the same name?
- No.

39:08.840 --> 39:10.120
I'm Xerxes Desai.

39:32.960 --> 39:34.000
Hello, sir.

39:39.040 --> 39:40.480
Akash Dixit.

39:41.480 --> 39:42.920
'Xerox' Desai.

39:43.840 --> 39:45.840
- Xerxes...
- Sir, it's Xerxes.

39:46.560 --> 39:48.440
'Zer-ka-sis', Xerxes.

39:50.200 --> 39:51.120
Sorry.

39:51.880 --> 39:53.000
How many do you want?

39:54.520 --> 39:57.800
Sir, can we see the options?

40:02.920 --> 40:03.720
All right.

40:16.280 --> 40:17.920
Sir, this one.

40:19.680 --> 40:22.400
This one and this one. All four.

40:23.080 --> 40:23.880
Ten units of each brand.

40:23.960 --> 40:26.720
So, all in all, it comes to 40,000.

40:28.480 --> 40:29.640
"40,000?"

40:30.120 --> 40:31.040
Yes, sir.

40:31.480 --> 40:32.920
Why do you need 40,000 watches?

40:33.440 --> 40:35.960
- We should leave.
- No, let me talk to him.

40:36.120 --> 40:37.440
He is a gangster.

40:37.680 --> 40:39.480
What are you whispering
to each other?

40:43.880 --> 40:45.120
Sir, um...

40:46.520 --> 40:51.000
Sir, we want to start
a small watch business.

40:51.120 --> 40:53.640
Selling vests and underwear
could make a small business,

40:54.360 --> 40:56.600
but trading in watches
could prove expensive.

40:57.520 --> 40:59.920
The watch business
is my biggest business.

41:00.640 --> 41:01.840
How big, sir?

41:04.880 --> 41:08.800
I mean,
what is your annual turnover?

41:10.600 --> 41:12.400
- No, sir...
- Are you an informant?

41:12.560 --> 41:17.120
No, we really want
to start a watch business.

41:17.160 --> 41:18.920
You know, Mumbai's artists,

41:19.400 --> 41:21.440
politicians making
statements in Parliament,

41:21.440 --> 41:24.800
big businessmen, advocates,
engineers, and doctors.

41:25.120 --> 41:28.320
They all wear my watches.

41:29.760 --> 41:30.960
Absolutely, sir.

41:31.080 --> 41:34.040
If you dare meddle in my business,
your delicate wrists

41:34.600 --> 41:36.360
won't even be able to carry bangles.

41:36.400 --> 41:37.880
- No, sir. I was just...
- Uh...

41:38.840 --> 41:40.080
We won't meddle.

41:40.600 --> 41:42.080
- It's cancelled.
- We're sorry, sir.

41:42.120 --> 41:43.280
- Thank you, sir.
- Sorry!

41:45.720 --> 41:46.880
Idiots.

41:52.160 --> 41:53.400
Come on, fast!

41:55.560 --> 41:57.640
- I hope we're not being followed.
- You messed up.

41:58.320 --> 41:59.520
"Forty thousand!"

42:05.600 --> 42:07.200
So, what's my role in this job?

42:07.880 --> 42:11.520
What's my salary,
and where's my cabin?

42:12.720 --> 42:13.960
Did you leave your job?

42:17.920 --> 42:18.960
Yes...

42:19.640 --> 42:22.200
Since you asked me to come, I came.

42:22.320 --> 42:24.800
No! No! No! I only asked

42:26.040 --> 42:27.480
for a one-off favour.

42:27.880 --> 42:29.760
I didn't ask you to quit your job.

42:30.480 --> 42:31.880
- Huh?
- Yes.

42:34.600 --> 42:35.840
I...

42:36.280 --> 42:38.200
I mean... Attitude...

42:38.800 --> 42:40.280
- No! No!
- What should I do now?

42:40.400 --> 42:41.800
- Hear me out.
- What will I do now?

42:41.840 --> 42:43.400
Listen to me.

42:44.000 --> 42:47.080
I don't even have Jeh's confirmation
for the watch project.

42:47.160 --> 42:49.680
- Huh...
- But if it's confirmed,

42:50.120 --> 42:51.640
then you're hired.

42:52.320 --> 42:55.120
Otherwise, you can rejoin NBIDC.

42:55.240 --> 42:57.320
Do you even know what I did there?

42:58.240 --> 42:59.480
'You will regret this.'

43:01.240 --> 43:02.280
'It's fine. I'll deal with it.'

43:02.720 --> 43:05.680
'I have zero interest
in your government job.'

43:08.680 --> 43:09.840
'All the best.'

43:10.120 --> 43:11.440
[in Spanish] 'Hasta la vista.'

43:12.120 --> 43:13.160
'Oh!'

43:20.560 --> 43:22.440
"Hasta la vista?"

43:24.320 --> 43:25.120
Oh, no.

43:25.840 --> 43:28.280
How will I face Dad,
Vihaan, and Kumud?

43:28.360 --> 43:29.440
Please don't panic.

43:29.560 --> 43:30.720
What do you mean?

43:30.800 --> 43:32.520
When you didn't even have
the basic confirmation,

43:32.640 --> 43:34.320
why did you ask me to come?

43:35.040 --> 43:37.000
- I want the confirmation right now.
Come with me. - Oi!

43:37.160 --> 43:38.600
- Come on.
- One second, please.

43:38.680 --> 43:39.480
The pitch is not ready.

43:39.520 --> 43:40.600
- It's not ready.
- Prepare it there.

43:40.600 --> 43:41.520
- Come with me immediately.
- Okay.

43:41.520 --> 43:42.680
Let me just confirm if he's there.

43:42.720 --> 43:44.680
Take Mr. J.R.D.'s confirmation.
Enough is enough.

43:44.720 --> 43:45.640
Okay.

43:48.760 --> 43:49.800
Hello, Operator.

43:50.720 --> 43:52.040
Yes. Bombay House, please.

43:52.680 --> 43:54.560
Yes. May I speak to Mr. Tata?

43:55.840 --> 43:58.240
Oi, Pinks! Yes, I'm good.

43:59.400 --> 44:00.280
How are you...

44:00.600 --> 44:02.680
Um, may I speak to J.R.D., please?

44:03.800 --> 44:04.760
Hi, Jeh!

44:05.280 --> 44:06.600
Jeh, I want to meet you.

44:06.720 --> 44:08.840
Zee, I'm leaving for Europe tonight.

44:08.960 --> 44:10.600
'I'll call you once I get there.'

44:11.640 --> 44:13.200
No, it's really important.

44:25.000 --> 44:26.240
- Let's go.
- Okay! Okay!

44:32.120 --> 44:33.040
Hey...

44:40.400 --> 44:41.440
All the best.

44:43.760 --> 44:45.160
Yes, thank you.

44:45.640 --> 44:47.080
- Give me a second, sir.
- Hi, Jeh!

44:47.400 --> 44:48.440
Make it quick.

44:48.880 --> 44:50.760
Tata Press cannot become profitable.

44:51.480 --> 44:52.720
So you're giving up the challenge.

44:52.760 --> 44:55.560
No! The challenge was
to rescue the press from losses.

44:55.840 --> 44:57.280
It wasn't about
making it profitable.

44:57.440 --> 44:59.680
Don't play with words.
Get to the point.

44:59.880 --> 45:04.320
Jeh, there are only two ways
to make the press profitable.

45:05.560 --> 45:06.800
One is an IPO.

45:07.120 --> 45:09.360
But where would we invest
the funds raised from the public?

45:09.800 --> 45:11.800
Will we buy more useless machines?

45:12.080 --> 45:13.360
What's the second option?

45:13.440 --> 45:14.440
Do you know about Nokia?

45:14.560 --> 45:15.520
Are you talking
about the paper mill?

45:15.640 --> 45:16.560
Not anymore.

45:16.640 --> 45:18.440
They're pivoting
to the cellphone business.

45:18.680 --> 45:19.800
Good for them. So?

45:19.880 --> 45:21.720
I also want to pivot away
from Tata Press.

45:21.840 --> 45:24.120
Just because Nokia is pivoting, it
doesn't mean we would do the same.

45:24.160 --> 45:25.960
I'm not copying them, Jeh.

45:26.640 --> 45:29.040
I went through and researched
all the files from the press.

45:29.080 --> 45:30.800
There's no scope.

45:31.040 --> 45:33.040
Press is a thing of the past.

45:33.640 --> 45:34.840
And what is the trend?

45:36.080 --> 45:37.560
- Watches?
- Yes!

45:37.640 --> 45:40.320
- Come on! You cannot be serious.
- I am!

45:42.320 --> 45:44.280
Listen, watchmaking

45:45.560 --> 45:48.240
is a difficult
and delicate business.

45:48.240 --> 45:49.280
You won't be able to do it.

45:49.280 --> 45:51.120
- So...
- Please hear me out.

45:51.520 --> 45:53.160
Please give me two minutes, Jeh.

45:53.240 --> 45:54.560
You have one minute.

45:54.960 --> 45:56.960
And your time starts now.

45:57.040 --> 45:58.680
Okay! You and the Tatas

45:58.960 --> 46:01.560
launched Lakmé
for the women of this country.

46:01.720 --> 46:04.000
A brand that changed
the way women see themselves.

46:04.160 --> 46:06.120
Lakmé was launched
for the country's 'Lakshmi',

46:06.240 --> 46:07.480
but what about the 'Narayanas'?

46:07.600 --> 46:11.080
There's no accessory
that represents their personality,

46:11.160 --> 46:13.880
status, and achievements.

46:14.040 --> 46:16.600
The one thing that can represent
all of those things is a wristwatch.

46:17.160 --> 46:20.080
Not a single premium watch
has ever been made in India.

46:20.480 --> 46:21.760
I want to make it.

46:22.280 --> 46:25.760
I don't want to make it just for
film stars, doctors, and lawyers,

46:25.800 --> 46:28.000
but for the common people of India.

46:28.080 --> 46:30.040
We'll make watches
not only for those

46:30.240 --> 46:33.000
who have good times,
but also for those

46:33.640 --> 46:35.520
who want to change their times.

46:37.000 --> 46:39.160
We are the best candidates
to do this, Jeh.

46:39.240 --> 46:42.840
- We can do this, and we must!
- And your one minute is over.

46:45.120 --> 46:47.320
I don't know about the watch,

46:47.360 --> 46:50.640
but your Hindi
has definitely improved.

46:51.560 --> 46:52.680
Jeh.

46:55.160 --> 46:56.200
Think about it.

47:04.520 --> 47:05.520
I don't know.

47:11.240 --> 47:12.200
I really don't know.

48:24.040 --> 48:25.400
- Good morning, sir.
- Good morning.

48:25.480 --> 48:28.080
What's my schedule
for tomorrow and the day after?

48:28.200 --> 48:29.320
Tomorrow is a day off, sir.

48:29.480 --> 48:31.520
- Hmm. - We'll meet the dealers
the day after tomorrow.

48:33.760 --> 48:34.920
So please arrange my meeting

48:35.560 --> 48:38.440
with the chairman
of Andre Jeuba for tomorrow.

48:38.640 --> 48:40.160
But he's in Switzerland.

48:40.240 --> 48:41.120
I know.

48:43.920 --> 48:46.360
I'll prepare the proposal letter
and schedule the meeting.

48:46.440 --> 48:47.880
- Right.
- Yes, sir.

49:00.840 --> 49:02.040
Mr. Tata.

49:04.000 --> 49:04.880
Come with me, Pinks.

49:05.840 --> 49:06.680
This way, please.

49:06.760 --> 49:09.160
[speaking French]

49:09.320 --> 49:12.640
[speaking French]

49:12.760 --> 49:15.120
[speaking French]

49:16.160 --> 49:17.280
[speaking French]

49:19.000 --> 49:21.440
Sir has read your proposal.

49:21.520 --> 49:23.000
Are the Indians

49:23.080 --> 49:25.800
really thinking
of making world-class watches?

49:26.120 --> 49:27.240
Absolutely.

49:27.520 --> 49:28.800
That's why

49:29.240 --> 49:33.000
we want to collaborate
with the world's finest watchmakers,

49:33.480 --> 49:34.800
Andre Jeuba.

49:34.880 --> 49:38.040
You know... In fact, your father
presented me with this one.

49:48.840 --> 49:52.040
We are making
the best watches in the world

49:52.080 --> 49:54.840
because we never compromise
on quality.

49:55.360 --> 49:56.160
Right.

49:57.600 --> 49:59.280
Look at this mechanism.

49:59.840 --> 50:02.400
[speaking French]

50:03.360 --> 50:05.120
[speaking French]

50:06.360 --> 50:07.480
Mr. Tata,

50:07.760 --> 50:10.560
Indian engineers know
how to make watches,

50:10.600 --> 50:14.480
but will they be able
to make world-class watches?

50:17.480 --> 50:21.680
See, we choose the best components
from all over the world

50:21.760 --> 50:25.200
and assemble them
precisely in the watch.

50:26.160 --> 50:27.600
That's how we make

50:27.840 --> 50:30.560
300 world-class watches every day.

50:31.080 --> 50:33.320
We produce a limited number
of watches, Mr. Tata,

50:33.600 --> 50:38.040
each with a precision
of five seconds.

50:38.520 --> 50:42.320
Can Indians really manufacture
world-class watches?

50:43.400 --> 50:47.360
[speaking French]

50:48.200 --> 50:52.080
[speaking French]

50:53.640 --> 50:57.160
We believe your answer
to all our questions is "no".

50:58.440 --> 51:02.480
Then why should we collaborate
with an Indian company?

51:04.200 --> 51:07.480
With all due respect, Mr. Tata,

51:09.040 --> 51:11.720
Indians don't know
how to manufacture watches.

51:12.800 --> 51:16.480
They lack talent and skill.

51:16.840 --> 51:18.120
They can only labour.

51:23.920 --> 51:26.040
Watches require skill.

51:27.000 --> 51:29.240
We can drink together.

51:30.160 --> 51:31.960
I can offer you

51:32.000 --> 51:34.120
the finest Swiss chocolate today,

51:35.280 --> 51:36.480
but not a deal.

51:41.480 --> 51:45.840
The designer of your best-selling
watches, Sita Meyer, is an Indian.

51:47.040 --> 51:49.720
Yet you doubt
the capabilities of Indians.

51:49.960 --> 51:54.080
I am 100% confident
we can make a world-class watch.

51:55.600 --> 51:57.520
We manufacture locomotives,

51:57.560 --> 51:59.480
steel plants, communication systems,

51:59.520 --> 52:01.200
and even aeroplanes,

52:01.960 --> 52:03.920
but your company doesn't.

52:06.160 --> 52:09.400
That's because your thinking
is small and constricted,

52:09.440 --> 52:11.400
just like your watches.

52:18.920 --> 52:21.080
[in French]
Thank you for the chocolate

52:21.920 --> 52:24.040
and for your time.

52:29.840 --> 52:32.000
Please translate everything
I've just said for him.

52:45.640 --> 52:47.760
I've been lying and coming here
for the past few days.

52:49.360 --> 52:52.280
I made a serious mistake
by leaving NBIDC.

52:55.920 --> 52:57.320
I want to go back to New Bombay.

52:57.360 --> 52:59.320
Then please go. Leave.

53:00.680 --> 53:02.840
You keep whinging all the time.
Anyway, you're losing.

53:03.680 --> 53:06.760
Don't use big English words
and infuriate me.

53:06.800 --> 53:07.840
I'm telling you. Or...

53:10.160 --> 53:11.160
Sir!

53:13.040 --> 53:15.440
Are you certain
you can make a watch?

53:15.680 --> 53:17.280
Jeh, what brings you here?

53:19.040 --> 53:20.520
I asked you a question.

53:21.680 --> 53:23.000
Can you make a watch?

53:24.960 --> 53:25.960
Yes.

53:26.440 --> 53:27.720
How much time will it take?

53:28.200 --> 53:29.360
I don't know.

53:29.880 --> 53:31.320
Maybe...

53:31.920 --> 53:32.960
Four or five years.

53:33.600 --> 53:34.800
Five years, it is.

53:35.720 --> 53:36.960
You know, I

53:38.040 --> 53:40.680
used to call this
a symbol of excellence.

53:42.640 --> 53:45.080
Actually, it's a symbol
of their arrogance.

53:45.640 --> 53:48.280
The Swiss watchmakers
don't consider Indians

53:48.320 --> 53:50.520
good enough to collaborate with.

53:54.760 --> 53:55.760
No problem.

53:56.920 --> 53:58.760
We will make watches
without collaborating with them.

54:00.960 --> 54:03.760
I want the finest watch
in the world,

54:03.960 --> 54:06.480
entirely made in India, in my hand.

54:09.000 --> 54:10.080
Until then,

54:13.520 --> 54:15.080
I will not wear a watch.

54:19.000 --> 54:19.960
Good luck!
